cmd/mygo: `mygo publish` uploads a build made before

`mygo build -upload` builds and uploads in one go. With updates.s3 the
upload publishes at once (apps see the update when its manifest is
there; there is no draft as on GitHub), so a release could not be checked
(signature, notarization, Gatekeeper) between the build and the moment
apps see it, and the files could not be renamed for a server that wants
other names (AudioSmith's site keeps its disk images as
<prefix>/AudioSmith-<version>.dmg).

`mygo publish [-platform …] [-o …] [dir]` uploads what `mygo build` left in
<out>/<goos>-<goarch> through the same publish() as -upload (GitHub draft
or S3, manifests last, the beta directory of patch 0008), under the
files' current names. It checks that every update manifest there is of
mygo.json's version, and refuses the web platform and missing builds.

Test: TestRunPublish (a renamed disk image, archive, delta and manifest of
a prerelease into beta/, skipping the bundle and dotfiles; another
version, no build, web).
